60,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Option B seems the most fluid, but it might increase the ""scramble"" and friction Shizue mentioned.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shizue,,I fear Option B might make the morning rush even more chaotic for the elderly. Option C feels very fair.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,May,,Option A is the only one that actually addresses the financial void. Let's make the building some money for once.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,George,,Option B is the only one that removes the need for a register or monthly tracking. It's the most sustainable.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Mio,,Option C is great because it breaks the cycle of the same people getting the spots! Everyone gets a chance!,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@May, a fee might create a divide between those who can pay and those who can't. That's not good for the atmosphere.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@George, if we have no assigned spots, I worry the bikes will be pushed into each other even more.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,May,,"@Misaki, it's a bicycle spot, not a luxury penthouse. A small fee is a perfectly reasonable way to allocate a scarce resource.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,George,,"@Shizue, a bit of physical reorganization is better than a permanent administrative nightmare. I'm sticking with B.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@May, I like the idea of paying, but I think a lottery is more exciting and fair for everyone!","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"Option C is a compromise. It's fair, it's periodic, and it doesn't create a financial hierarchy.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I agree with Misaki. A lottery is a gentle way to ensure everyone has a turn without any one person feeling left out.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,May,,You're all being too soft. Option A is the only professional way to handle this. Why are we afraid of a small fee?,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,George,,"Because someone has to collect that fee, May. I've seen these ""small fees"" turn into a bookkeeping disaster.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Mio,,"I'm definitely going with the lottery! It's the best way to clear out the old ""reserved"" spots!","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Misaki,,I'll vote for the lottery. It's the least likely to cause long-term resentment if everyone knows the rules are random.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Shizue,,I will also vote for the lottery. Let's keep the peace and give everyone a fair chance.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,May,,"Fine, if you all want to keep the building broke, go ahead. But I'm voting for the paid system.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,George,,I'll stick with the shared racks. It's the only one that doesn't require a manager.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Mio,,Yay! Lottery it is! Let's shake things up!,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
